  "implementation": [
    "Decode a complete Q8_0 block span in the existing native decoder with AVX2 signed-byte widening and F16C half-scale conversion",
    "Convert each group of eight signed bytes to exact binary32 integers, multiply by the block scale once in binary32, and write all 32 values before advancing 34 input and 128 output bytes",
    "Keep the block loop inside the kernel and clear upper vector state once at the end; the original scalar decoder remains the fallback",
    "Use the existing x86-64-v3 guard, which requires both AVX2 and F16C, and retain existing source/target/count refusal checks before entering the kernel",
    "Keep model quantization, accumulation/reduction order, physical weights, workspaces and session lifecycle unchanged; no persistent cache, new runtime or threads"
  ],
